# Konnen Computer das Sprachproblem losen (Can Computers Solve the Language Problem)?

**Authors:** Zeilinger, Michael

## Abstract
Various computer applications in linguistics, primarily speech synthesis and machine translation, are reviewed. Although the computer proves useful for statistics, dictionary building and programmed instruction, the promulgation of a world auxiliary language is considered a more human and practical solution to the international communication problem. (Text is in German.) Available from Humanities Press, Inc., Atlantic Highlands, NJ 07716. (TL)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ122801

